            <ArticleTitle>Two {Dy2} single-molecule magnets formed via an in situ reaction by capturing CO2 from atmosphere under ambient conditions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1753-1756</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6dt04751c</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Under ambient conditions, CO2 was captured from atmosphere and reduced for sequestering CO2 into two {Dy2} single-molecule magnets through an in situ organic ligand reaction of hydrazine. A reasonable reaction mechanism is proposed, which provides a promising route towards the capturing and transforming CO2 into single-molecule magnets.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
